{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\nFollows from the implication (a) $\\Rightarrow$ (b) in\n\\cite[IV, Corollary 1.10.4]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$\\varphi : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0004": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-generizing}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d11e4245219bdc7adbcf0255e12a103633f28c48175a74516060fee8cdba13bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:644f8b3b2544bf4e48ff21d33240b9550664ce0527f8d6d7bd63c2fc0daf3dc9", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0002> is open, then <MATH_0003> is generizing\n(i.e., generalizations lift along <MATH_0004>).\nIf <MATH_0005> is universally open, then <MATH_0006> is\nuniversally generizing.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b5c38d4ed9b3101ecf7b3cd93d4a644c2a9cdc72f1af4c88954b66f982bda99b", "unit_id": "tag:040F:statement"}
